Consumer perception of remanufactured products is often dominated by age assumptions (older = worse) rather than actual performance capability. Performance equivalence labelling overcomes this perception gap by providing objective evidence. Clear performance documentation enables consumers to make rational purchasing decisions based on actual capabilities rather than age bias.

Performance data communicates confidence manufacturers have in remanufactured products. Visible equivalence information creates conditions where remanufactured products compete fairly with new products on performance basis. Test-based labelling builds credibility that simple marketing claims cannot achieve.